      "original": "$\\frac{\\Delta l}{l}=\\beta\\Delta t$",
      "corrected": "",
      "reason": "Independent D016 SCI source finding: p0140#5 explicitly defines relative expansion as Delta l/l_0 and p0140#9 gives l=l_0(1+beta Delta t). The printed equation7-1 denominator l instead implies l=l_0/(1-beta Delta t), inconsistent with that declared reference-length model. OpenStax College Physics2e13.2, read through CloakBrowser on2026-11-16, gives Delta L=alpha L Delta T using the initial reference length for the small-temperature-range linear model. Correct only this exact math token to denominator l_0 in the modern edition, preserve all printed source blocks/rows/figures and the original formula. Reference: https://openstax.org/books/college-physics-2e/pages/13-2-thermal-expansion-of-solids-and-liquids."
    }
